WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.511
Hi, and thank you for helping us test Concord.

2
00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.675
In about three minutes I'll show you how the alpha works,

3
00:00:07.675 --> 00:00:10.485
and the easiest ways to tell us what you think.

4
00:00:11.286 --> 00:00:13.236
Everything starts on this page.

5
00:00:13.236 --> 00:00:16.371
It explains what Concord is for, and it has a short tour

6
00:00:16.371 --> 00:00:19.828
of the whole platform if you'd like the bigger picture.

7
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.080
Taking part has four steps.

8
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.191
Pick a role, try a few tasks, let the simulated

9
00:00:26.191 --> 00:00:29.419
participants act, and then tell us what you think.

10
00:00:29.419 --> 00:00:31.444
There's no account to create.

11
00:00:32.245 --> 00:00:35.119
When you're ready, press Start the guided walkthrough.

12
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.335
The walkthrough saves your place in this browser,

13
00:00:38.335 --> 00:00:41.380
so you can stop and come back whenever you like.

14
00:00:42.181 --> 00:00:44.143
First, choose a role.

15
00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:47.998
You could be the steward who looks after a standard, a domain expert,

16
00:00:47.998 --> 00:00:52.874
a voting member, someone from the ODI, or a developer building on it.

17
00:00:52.874 --> 00:00:55.138
Here, I'll be a voting member.

18
00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.564
Each role has a few people to choose from.

19
00:00:58.564 --> 00:01:02.523
You play that person, and everyone else around you is simulated.

20
00:01:03.324 --> 00:01:07.271
Next, the walkthrough suggests a few things to try in that role.

21
00:01:07.271 --> 00:01:11.944
Press Go to open the right page, and tick each task off when you're done.

22
00:01:12.746 --> 00:01:16.508
If you'd rather explore on your own, keep the guide open.

23
00:01:16.508 --> 00:01:20.452
It sits in the corner of every page, so you won't lose your place.

24
00:01:21.252 --> 00:01:23.934
Real governance takes days, or weeks.

25
00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:29.324
So press Simulate the others, and the other participants comment, review and vote.

26
00:01:30.573 --> 00:01:36.006
Then move the clock forward a day or a week, so reviews close and votes are counted.

27
00:01:37.308 --> 00:01:41.650
The demo is shared with the other testers, so you may see their work too.

28
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.126
Please don't type in anything confidential.

29
00:01:44.925 --> 00:01:48.530
When you've seen enough, there are two ways to give feedback.

30
00:01:49.493 --> 00:01:52.210
Guided feedback takes about eight minutes.

31
00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:56.436
An assistant asks a short set of questions about each part of Concord,

32
00:01:56.436 --> 00:01:59.420
including how you'd want its decisions to be made.

33
00:02:00.222 --> 00:02:01.952
Or just tell us something.

34
00:02:01.952 --> 00:02:05.365
A bug, an idea, or something that confused you.

35
00:02:05.365 --> 00:02:08.189
Type it, or tap the microphone and talk.

36
00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:11.742
The assistant may ask a follow-up question or two.

37
00:02:11.742 --> 00:02:14.006
Say as much or as little as you like.

38
00:02:17.159 --> 00:02:21.887
When you're done, press Submit, and it goes straight to the team building Concord.

39
00:02:22.688 --> 00:02:25.521
You don't have to finish the walkthrough first.

40
00:02:25.521 --> 00:02:27.901
Give feedback is at the top of every page,

41
00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:31.961
so tell us the moment something surprises you, good or bad.

42
00:02:32.762 --> 00:02:34.364
Thanks again for your time.

43
00:02:34.364 --> 00:02:38.091
Honest reactions help us most, so please don't hold back.
